window.COPY={"a2h-baptist":{"txt":"Baptist Memorial Hospital-Fayette County is a community hospital that holds emergency treatment, inpatient care and diagnostic services under one roof. The planned program includes eight emergency beds, eight inpatient beds, telehealth, imaging and laboratory services. A2H's architecture and engineering keep the building compact: a glass-fronted lobby and a covered emergency drop-off put public arrival and waiting directly beside the clinical spaces for emergency care and short hospital stays.","sub":"Public and clinical spaces","det":"The lobby, nurse station and dining area share one palette of wood tones and blue accents. Full-height glazing lights the lobby, a blue-framed nurse station opens onto the staff work area, and a small dining room sits behind a glass corner. The three rooms cover the range of settings in the planned hospital, from patient and visitor arrival to clinical work and smaller gatherings.","area":"18,233 SF","scope":"Proposed hospital / CON filing"},"a2h-didd":{"txt":"This regional office and support campus in Arlington serves state programs for Tennesseans with disabilities. A2H provided architecture and engineering for the West Tennessee Regional Office. The 15-acre campus, opened in March 2026, holds three buildings: administration, a seating and positioning clinic, and maintenance and warehouse. Each building has its own identity, and landscape and circulation tie them together. Deep roof overhangs mark the entries, and glass-lined corridors look onto shared lawns.","sub":"A campus of related facilities","det":"The regional office sits among the campus's supporting buildings and landscape. Each building carries its own architectural character within the setting they share.","area":"15-acre campus","scope":"Floor-area total unresolved"},"a2h-covington":{"txt":"Covington's elementary and middle school campus was rebuilt after the March 2023 tornado. A2H's work with Tipton County Schools pairs classrooms fitted with current technology with updated safety features and shared spaces. Outside, each school has its own prominent entrance, and a steady rhythm of light and dark vertical bands runs across the facade, tying the two schools into one campus for students and the wider community."},"a2h-houston":{"txt":"This addition to Houston Middle School expands specialized learning and athletics and creates a secure entrance on Johnson Road. It holds a 1,100-seat competition gymnasium, band facilities, two art rooms and three STEM classrooms. Tall gridded windows between brick piers form a glazed public frontage that marks the addition on campus. The addition opened in January 2023.","sub":"Spaces for making and learning","det":"Inside, each kind of specialized learning gets a room with its own identity. A high-ceiling band room has space for colorguard practice, the expanded art facilities include pottery kilns, and the STEM rooms support flexible teaching. The competition gym doubles the previous seating capacity, so the addition serves larger school gatherings as well as everyday classes.","area":"42,974 SF","scope":"Addition"},"a2h-thompson":{"txt":"The Thompson Machinery regional headquarters is a campus in Collierville that sets the main building, service facilities and rental operations on one coordinated site plan. Each building has its own identity, yet dark metal panels, wood-toned accents and a covered front walk make them read as one family. Workplace, service frontage, circulation and landscape fit together across the larger equipment campus.","sub":"Workplace within an equipment campus","det":"The headquarters is tied to the service and rental facilities around it. Differences in scale and frontage tell visitors what each building does, while the shared architectural family holds the group together. Buildings, access routes and landscaped areas work as parts of one site.","area":"174,970 SF main building","scope":"Component / design documentation"},"a2h-dresden":{"txt":"The Dresden Municipal Complex is a new home for the city's municipal services. Following the December 2021 tornado, A2H helped assess damaged city facilities and designed the replacement, which opened in May 2025. City hall, police and fire departments share a paved entry court, with dedicated workspaces, flexible meeting areas and a public community safe space.","sub":"Shared needs, distinct departments","det":"The program includes a courtroom, firefighter sleeping quarters, a police patrol room, evidence storage and records rooms. Flexible shared spaces serve several departments, and the community safe space responds directly to the disaster behind the project. The courtyard, a glass-lined corridor and the apparatus bay mark the different scales of this combined civic program.","area":"17,824 SF","scope":"Building"},"a2h-oosm":{"txt":"Oxford Orthopaedics & Sports Medicine is organized around a tall glazed entry tower and a covered arrival. The tower gives the practice an address patients can recognize from the parking lot, and the canopy shelters them at the door. Inside, the arrival continues through reception, waiting and a feature stair. Brick and light panels wrap the two-story clinic wings on either side of the tower.","sub":"From arrival to the interior","det":"The feature stair climbs inside the glass tower, so the entrance carries straight into the interior. Reception and waiting take the same daylight and materials at a smaller scale, with wood doors, a dark reception desk and floor-to-ceiling glass along the waiting area.","area":"27,000 GSF","scope":"Archived design / 2020"},"a2h-orthosouth":{"txt":"This 26,074-square-foot outpatient surgery center and pain-management clinic is part of a wider repositioning of the Exeter medical campus in Germantown. It sits below OrthoSouth's main orthopaedic practice and extends the building's healthcare program with dedicated patient-facing and clinical spaces. A2H's architecture and interior design lead patients from a covered drop-off and glass entry into waiting, recovery and treatment areas within the existing facility.","sub":"A renewed outpatient environment","det":"Patient waiting, recovery and clinical workspaces extend the orthopaedic program inside the existing building. Wood-toned walls, a curved reception desk and easy transitions from one space to the next give patients and staff a consistent outpatient environment. The surgery center is one piece of a wider campus renovation effort spanning ten related subprojects.","area":"26,074 SF","scope":"Expanded ASC tenant space"},"a2h-marshall":{"txt":"This 8,000-square-foot health center replaces an aging county facility with examination rooms, medical offices, community space and supporting functions. Familiar rural building forms are paired with contemporary materials, and an extended roofline shelters the entrance and shows visitors where to arrive. A timber trellis shades the front walk. Clinical care and community programming share one building serving Lewisburg and Marshall County.","area":"7,995 SF","scope":"Building"},"a2h-unioncity":{"txt":"This 24,000-square-foot medical office building adds women's health and cardiology services to the Union City hospital campus. Developed with Big River Development for Baptist Medical Group, it holds a ground-floor women's health center, with Stern Cardiology occupying the remaining space. A covered entrance and a two-story glazed corner mark the public arrival and give patients a sheltered drop-off.","sub":"A focused clinical program","det":"The 12,000-square-foot women's health center includes 18 examination rooms, two procedure rooms, two ultrasound suites, a laboratory and conference space. Being on the hospital campus places these outpatient services alongside a broader range of care. An open stair rises inside the glazed corner, so arrival and the route upstairs share the same daylit space.","area":"24,000 SF","scope":"Two-story building"},"a2h-olivebranch":{"txt":"This low-rise medical office building gives outpatient care in Olive Branch a clear presence of its own. Brick and dark masonry volumes, a glazed entrance and a projecting canopy shape the public front, so patients can spot the door from the parking area and be dropped off under cover. Inside, the waiting room looks back out through that same glass, and wood floors and dark trim carry the exterior palette indoors."},"a2h-millington-cte":{"txt":"This career and technical education building extends the architectural identity of the Millington school campus. A long frontage ends in a corner entrance framed in gold, which carries the school name and mascot and gives the building a recognizable public face. The site plan places it among the existing school buildings, beside the track."},"a2h-milan-park":{"txt":"The McKellar Park master plan sets playgrounds, courts, a skate park and open recreation space in one connected public landscape in Milan. Looping walking routes, parking and a pavilion organize how people arrive and gather, linking activities that need very different kinds of space. The park sits within its neighborhood, with houses on the surrounding streets.","sub":"Places for play and gathering","det":"The playground, skate park and courts are distinct destinations within the larger plan. Different surfaces, equipment and edges give each activity its own setting, from colorful climbing mounds to concrete bowls and rails. Paths and shared open areas connect these recreation spaces.","area":"Approximately 8 acres"},"a2h-caruthersville":{"txt":"This adaptive reuse of the 1916 Exchange Building supports the revitalization of downtown Caruthersville. A2H's proposal combines events and gallery space, Chamber of Commerce offices and upper-floor uses, while addressing accessibility, code deficiencies and project phasing. Restoration and an addition link the brick building's historic street frontage to interior gathering spaces and an outdoor edge with a patio, pergola and murals.","sub":"Historic fabric and new gathering space","det":"The renovation and addition create 8,560 square feet of programmed space. A2H also assisted with grant planning, and the first-floor uses support the arts council, public events and the Chamber of Commerce. A solarium and patio carry the public program out from the historic building.","area":"8,560 SF","scope":"Renovation and addition"},"a2h-southaven":{"txt":"Southaven Fire Station No. 5 gives an essential public service a distinct presence along its street. A prominent tower marked with the station number, masonry walls and layered roof forms make the building easy to recognize from the road, with the arched apparatus bay doors off to one side."},"a2h-tipton":{"txt":"The Tipton County Animal Shelter in Brighton pairs public reception with dedicated animal-care areas. Outside, gabled roofs and bright red panels point visitors to the entrance. Inside, the red carries through to the service window of a daylit reception area, with cat rooms and kennel areas beyond."},"a2h-northdelta":{"txt":"This multipurpose building is an addition to the existing North Delta School facilities in Batesville. A large main volume in the school's green sits beside the football field, and a glazed entrance gives students and visitors a clear place to arrive and ties the building back to the rest of campus."},"a2h-vumc":{"txt":"This modular MRI building for Vanderbilt University Medical Center in Nashville is a compact clinical box, so the design work went into the skin: a clear front door for patients and a presence on the site for a small building. A glass door under a suspended canopy, with the sign right beside it, tells people where to go.","sub":"Facade study","det":"Several exterior schemes for the one building were rendered from the same viewpoint so they could be compared directly: smooth panels, a gridded panel pattern with a siding band, a brick base under light panels, and brick on every side with a panel cornice above. Every option keeps the same entry."},"a2h-bmg":{"txt":"The Exeter BMG imaging suite is part of the conversion of the former Baptist Rehab Hospital into a medical office campus. Within that larger renovation, the suite has its own arrival, waiting and reception. Wood tones, a stone-faced reception desk and light finishes run through the public rooms and tie them to the rest of the renovated campus.","sub":"Arrival, reception and waiting","det":"Patients enter through a glazed lobby and reach a reception desk set beside a wood-clad column. Wood marks the key elements, while light walls carry through to the adjoining waiting room, where seating lines the windows.","area":"4,023 SF","scope":"Tenant planning area / 2020"},"a2h-millington-mp":{"txt":"This schematic design is a multipurpose addition within an existing school campus. A large shared hall anchors the plan, with supporting rooms including classrooms and an ROTC space, and a link to surrounding school facilities such as the existing gymnasium. The exterior and the presentation plan set the relationship between the main volume, its entrance and the campus, giving early planning decisions an architectural direction for discussion.","area":"10,396 SF hall","scope":"Component only / schematic"},"a2h-bolivar":{"txt":"The Bolivar NeighborHub is a community workspace that sets open work areas and enclosed meeting rooms in one shared setting. Glass-fronted rooms and a larger room with rows of tables beside tall windows give people a range of places to work and gather. Furniture, finishes and glazing make the plan easy to read."},"a2h-waste":{"txt":"The office and operations project for Waste Connections in Memphis carries one architectural character through its public and staff spaces. A glazed entrance pavilion under a sloped roof sets up the arrival, and a covered patio with raised planters sits alongside. Inside, the lobby, meeting and break areas set wood feature walls against white surfaces, with exposed steel joists overhead tying the administrative side to the operational setting."},"a2h-milanpb":{"txt":"The Milan Public Works Building is a maintenance facility that pairs a substantial working volume with a clearly defined public entrance. A strong sloping roofline and a long service frontage of glazed overhead doors express the building's working character, while glazing marks where visitors arrive."},"a2h-soccer":{"txt":"The Milan Soccer Complex is a planning study that sets playing fields, walking routes, parking and supporting landscape on one site plan. An entry drive leads through trees to parking and shelters set right beside the fields. The fields form the main structure of the landscape, with access and shared space arranged around them."},"a2h-henderson":{"txt":"The new Henderson County Health Department expands space for examination, consultation, laboratory work and community education. Clinical services and public learning share one building, meant to strengthen local access to care. A deep entry canopy and a raised band of windows above it make the front door easy to find, and low sloped roofs fall away on either side. The replacement facility was designed to the county's service needs and to careful use of state and county investment."},"a2h-shelby":{"txt":"The Shelby County Center for Safety & Justice in Memphis is designed to support people in the justice system who face mental health challenges. A2H led the design with national and local partners. The program holds evaluation, counseling, short-term stabilization and discharge planning, connecting immediate support with planning for continuing care beyond the facility. A two-story glass entry under a floating roof gives the low masonry building an open front."},"a2h-overland":{"txt":"The Memphis Overland Building is a two-story brick building at 421 Monroe Avenue in Memphis, studied here for reuse. The storefronts reopen with new glass and the brick and terra cotta trim are cleaned, so people on the street can see into the building again. A small canopy marks the door on the corner, and tall windows on both floors bring daylight deep inside.","sub":"Facade study","det":"The storefront and window frames were tested in white, green and dark finishes against the existing brick. In 2020 the building stood with most of its openings closed up."},"x-blue":{"txt":"Blue Ridge is a set of exterior studies for a multi-story medical office building. A stone-clad tower marks the corner and carries the signage, while bands of glass and light panels wrap the upper floors. Patients arrive at a covered drop-off at the front door, with surface parking close by and a parking deck next to the building."},"a2h-anderson":{"txt":"This master plan lays out a residential development in Brownsville, Tennessee. Homes and townhouses sit around a clubhouse, pool and play areas, and lawns and walking paths connect each row to the shared amenities. A small commercial corner at the entrance gives the development a face on the street. Sport courts and a pavilion sit between the townhouse rows."},"a2h-astoria":{"txt":"Astoria Square is a mixed-use development in Millington, Tennessee, where apartments and hotel rooms sit above shops and restaurants. The buildings gather around a central green and a covered stage. A restaurant patio opens onto the lawn, with outdoor tables facing the stage and the hotel rising beyond it."},"a2h-benson":{"txt":"Benson Martin is a residential subdivision plan and its entrance. A brick entry sign sits in a planted island and leads onto a tree-lined street with sidewalks and lamp posts. Beyond it, winding roads carry the lots across open green parcels, with homes spread along them."},"a2h-carlisle":{"txt":"This new industrial facility sits on a large, open site. Visitors and staff arrive at an entry marked by a blue sign canopy and a stone base, with a wide glass storefront set between them. Beyond the entry, the plant, the truck courts and the tree-lined employee parking fill out the property."},"a2h-carroll":{"txt":"This farmers market pavilion sits at the Carroll County fairgrounds in Tennessee. Open vendor bays run along its front between brick piers, and a covered hall holds long tables for market days and community events. A wood-lined ceiling follows the pitch of the roof, giving shoppers and vendors shade and shelter."},"a2h-frayser":{"txt":"Frayser-Trezevant is a new 270,000 SF community high school for 1,500 students in Memphis that moves two existing high schools onto one campus; it is scheduled to open for the 2027-28 school year. The design development scheme centers on a learning stair, where students sit and gather on wide wooden tiers, and extends to the front approach, the entry plaza and the courtyard. The earlier schematic concept is included as well: the campus from the air, the courtyard stair tower and the gym entry.","area":"270,000 SF"},"a2h-hardin":{"txt":"This is a correctional training facility in Hardin County, Tennessee. The long, low building has a brick base and a green metal roof, with a secure yard at one end. Wide windows face the approach, and the fenced yard gives vehicles and equipment a protected place right beside the building."},"a2h-overton":{"txt":"This small project is a seating and planter wall at the edge of new parking for the Memphis Zoo in Overton Park. The retaining wall is stepped to make a bench, a planter and a stair, so people walking in from the lot have a place to stop on the way. Light masonry, flowering beds and a handrail along the bench keep it comfortable and easy to use beneath the park's trees."},"grec-222":{"txt":"Randolph Plaza is GREC's design proposal for The John Buck Company at 222 West Randolph: a 40-story, 1,000,000 SF office tower in the Chicago Loop. At street level the glass base opens the lobby to the sidewalk, and its glowing yellow art wall is visible from outside. Higher up, a planted sky lobby is set into the glass facade, a room with trees and long views over the city."},"grec-akh":{"txt":"Akhdar Green City is a master plan for a new coastal city. Neighborhoods cluster on the headland around green corridors, with a marina and waterfront district along the shore. Seen from the air, the rounded neighborhood clusters fan out from the center toward the hills behind, and waterways thread between them down to the sea."},"grec-ch":{"txt":"Chicago and Hudson is a residential tower at Chicago Avenue and Hudson in Chicago. A brick and glass base holds the street edge, with storefront glass along the sidewalk. The apartment tower rises behind it in a lighter skin of glass and metal and stands among the taller buildings of the surrounding skyline."},"grec-china":{"txt":"Zhong Shan Shun Xiang is a mixed-use development in China with office towers, retail and a hotel. Two angled glass office towers and a hotel block rise from a shared base, where the shopping center sits under ribbons of landscaped roof. Entries, terraces and gardens are worked into that base, so people can move between the three uses without leaving the site."},"grec-golf":{"txt":"A resort hotel at the Abu Dhabi golf course. Stone-clad wings step down toward terraces and pools, and winged roofs lift above the upper floors. Guests arrive under a broad stone entry canopy off a paved court."},"grec-kimp":{"txt":"Two of the most public spaces of a Kimpton hotel. Inside, a richly colored lobby lounge gathers sofas and bright rugs beside a wall of tall windows. Outside, the street entry sits under a glass canopy at the base of the tower, with an outdoor dining terrace that puts tables and umbrellas along the sidewalk."},"grec-king":{"txt":"Kingsbury is a residential tower on a corner site in Chicago. Brick and glass rise from a base of storefront glass, with trees along the sidewalk. Above the street, a landscaped terrace holds shaded tables, planting and a fountain, and a glass-walled dining room faces the skyline at night."},"grec-kp":{"txt":"Khalifa Park is a master plan for a 130-acre park in Abu Dhabi, organized around a central water body with gardens, plazas and pavilions along its edge. Paths and crossings circle the water, leading visitors between the districts from one group of pavilions and gardens to the next."},"grec-levy":{"txt":"Club and concession interiors for the stadium in Tampa, planned around how fans spend a game day. A team-branded club lounge seats ticket holders between red draped bays, a bar keeps the game in view on large screens, and a concession stand on the concourse carries signage bold enough to find in a crowd."},"bf-4320":{"txt":"An existing brick building at 4320 West Madison in Chicago becomes loft apartments with a gymnasium. The apartments keep the tall ceilings, exposed brick and open ductwork of the old building. Kitchens open onto the living rooms, and large multi-pane windows light the bedrooms. The gymnasium sits under white steel trusses and skylights, ringed by brick walls and a railed walkway at the upper level."},"bf-flow":{"txt":"Flow is a branded convenience store concept for Los Angeles, covering the exterior, the sales floor and the service counter. A curved gray canopy and bright green signs make the store easy to spot from the street. Inside, a green line in the floor leads shoppers past snacks, coolers and a coffee island to a glass-fronted counter for liquor and money services."},"bf-hyd":{"txt":"Hydrate is a bar interior in Chicago, kept dark so the bar itself draws people in. An island bar with a lit front sits at the center of the room, backed by a glowing bottle display. Wood floors and screens along the walls leave open space all around it, so guests can gather on every side."},"bf-lark":{"txt":"Lark is a bar and restaurant in Chicago. A dark paneled storefront with wide windows lets passersby see in from the sidewalk. Inside, a long carved wood bar runs along one wall over a herringbone floor, and a fireplace lounge with soft chairs sits apart from the bar."},"bf-nywf":{"txt":"New York Wing Factory is a restaurant and bar interior in Chicago, built for watching a game over a meal. A wood-fronted bar runs under a row of screens, with pendant bulbs and wood ceiling panels overhead. A dining room with red booths lines the brick wall opposite, where more screens keep every table in view of the action."},"bf-rav":{"txt":"Ravinia 555 is a set of apartment interiors: an open living room and kitchen with a stone island, and a bedroom. Wood-look floors and pale cabinets keep the rooms bright, and wide windows look out to the trees. The interiors were drawn before the units were built, so a future tenant could judge the finishes and the daylight in advance."},"bf-replay":{"txt":"Re-Play is an arcade bar in Chicago where the games share the room with the drinks. The long bar is backed by lit shelving and scoreboards on a brick wall, with arcade cabinets along the room's edge. Metal stools line the bar under hanging glass pendants, and a strip of light runs beneath the bar top."},"bf-rpa":{"txt":"Replay Andersonville is an arcade bar in Chicago's Andersonville neighborhood. A wood-clad bar sits at the center under a slatted ceiling, with rows of arcade cabinets and pinball machines along the brick walls. Seating wraps the bar on every side, within sight of the screens overhead and the games."},"kg-asc":{"txt":"A new cemetery administration building and site in Libertyville, Illinois. Gabled wings with dark metal roofs step along the drive and end in a round glazed room beneath a small cupola. Covered drop-offs at the entries give families a sheltered place to arrive. Parking, walks and a pond surround the building."},"kg-assum":{"txt":"A crypt and columbarium building in Wheaton, Illinois. A glazed gable entry sits between long walls of crypt fronts in brick and stone. Inside, the chapel hall rises to a wood ceiling and opens to rooms of lit niches where families can visit, with a cross set into the glass at each gable end."},"kg-cath":{"txt":"A church interior renovation paired with a new parish reception area. In the church, wood beams, white brick and stained glass windows frame the pews, and a white marble platform lifts the altar beneath the crucifix. In the reception area, a long marble desk stands in front of a wood wall of carved figures."},"kg-hf":{"txt":"A stone chapel mausoleum and a new entrance for a cemetery. The chapel's open timber porch frames a shrine wall, with pointed arch panels set into the stone on either side. From the entry drive, stone gate piers and a low fence open to a first sight of the chapel across the grounds."},"kg-hnd":{"txt":"Concept options for a chapel in a wooded setting in McHenry County, Illinois. Three were modeled for the client to compare on the same site: a round domed chapel, a columned temple and a modern pavilion. Each sits among the same trees and lawn, so the differences in shape and character are easy to judge."},"kg-niu":{"txt":"New dugouts and field-side improvements serve the softball program at Northern Illinois University. Each dugout carries a railed viewing deck on its roof, so the game can be watched from above the bench as well as from the stands. Brick end walls, wood benches and Huskies red match the dugouts to the rest of the ballpark."},"kg-qoh":{"txt":"A garden crypt complex at a cemetery in Hillside, Illinois, organized as walled courtyards around a lawn and a stained glass focal wall. A path leads from the entrance drive into the courts, where families walk and stop. Pale stone walls, marble crypt fronts, planting beds and benches line the courts, which stay open to the sky."},"kg-sj":{"txt":"A garden crypt courtyard at a cemetery. Stone piers and a glass canopy shelter the walks between crypt walls, and a statue and fountain mark the center where visitors arrive. Benches and planting line the walks, and daylight comes through the canopy overhead."},"kg-sme":{"txt":"A garden crypt wall and shrine for Saint Mary cemetery in Elmhurst, Illinois. Brick walls of crypt fronts step out from a central gabled shrine, giving families a clear place to arrive and a place to pause. A statue stands before the arched center bay, and a paved walk with flower beds runs the length of the wall."},"kg-stmary":{"txt":"An administration building of low stone volumes gathered around a taller tower topped with a cross, with stained glass set into the walls. Inside, skylights and colored glass light the gathering rooms, and a few armchairs give visitors a place to sit and wait. A crucifix hangs on a wood-paneled wall in the main room."},"mca-30":{"txt":"30 Court is a residential building in Morristown, New Jersey, and these are its shared amenity interiors. The lounge is built around a media wall, the dining room sits under a wood ceiling crossed by dark beams, and the lobby connects the two. Vertical wood slats line the walls of all three rooms, and globe chandeliers hang over the seating and the tables."},"mca-pad":{"txt":"The Evanston Paddle Club is a clubhouse interior with a bar and a fireplace lounge. Timber trusses and a plank ceiling run over both spaces, and large windows keep the courts and trees in view. Leather chairs gather at the stone fireplace, a few steps from the bar."},"mca-prin":{"txt":"The clubhouse interiors for a residential community. A two-story lounge holds sofas, a billiards table and a see-through fireplace under a wood ceiling. A quieter sitting room sits on the far side of the hearth, and a cafe bar runs along a marble-look counter with booth seating opposite."},"mek-as":{"txt":"A cemetery chapels and administration complex in Des Plaines, Illinois, carried from schematic design through construction drawings. A long covered entry leads families into a lobby that links three chapels of different sizes, a meet and greet room and private family rooms beside the offices. Outside, pale block walls curve gently and tall panels of stained glass mark the chapel end."},"mek-bron":{"txt":"A mausoleum building set into a sloping cemetery lawn in Oak Brook, Illinois. The classical front faces the drive, with a columned porch and carved pediment under a green metal roof. At the rear, a lower level opens to the slope down a railed walk. The building was studied in daylight and at dusk to test how it sits on the hill at different hours."},"mek-fr":{"txt":"A committal shelter and an administration building studied for Fort Rosecrans in San Diego. The shelter gives families a covered place to gather for a service, with stacked stone piers holding a low curved metal roof over benches. The administration building carries the same stone and curved red roofs, so the two read as one family along the cemetery drive."},"mek-hsm":{"txt":"A garden mausoleum complex at Holy Sepulchre Cemetery in Cook County, Illinois. Crypt buildings fan out from a round central court topped by a glass skylight, with small gardens and benches between them for visitors. The approach walk passes through pale stone piers into the court, and the outer crypt walls curve along a garden path."},"mek-hso":{"txt":"Garden crypt buildings at Holy Sepulcher Cemetery in Orange, California. Long terraced crypt walls step along the drive, faced in green stone and broken by stone piers. Partway along, the wall opens into a statue court with a small fountain where families can gather."},"mek-il93":{"txt":"At Motorola's Libertyville campus, the corporate cafeteria was remodeled with a branded servery, cafe counters and several kinds of seating, from window tables to lounge chairs along a curved balcony. Red stools and pale wood tabletops fill the dining floor, and a round canopy hangs over the coffee bar."},"mek-mill":{"txt":"These corporate office interiors for Milestone start at a double-height reception, where a red feature wall runs beside the desk and a glass-railed balcony looks down on it. A rounded corridor hub with a small lounge follows. Beyond that, a cafe and meeting space with bright mixed chairs sits beside an open stair."},"mek-oliv":{"txt":"A mausoleum and memorial garden. The building's arched front frames a mural of a lake in autumn, with round windows above the two entry arches. In front, the garden steps down in concentric rings around a central fountain, and a pergola at the top of the slope gives visitors a shaded place to pause."},"mek-pa06":{"txt":"The corporate cafeteria and servery at Motorola Mobility in Horsham were remodeled around a curved white wall that marks the entry to the cafe. The dining room opens behind it with wood floors and tall windows. Round ceiling clouds, a teal banquette wrapped around a column and red fabric canopies near the glass break the large room into smaller places to sit."},"mek-res":{"txt":"Crypt and niche buildings at Resurrection Cemetery in Justice, Illinois. Low buildings wrap a curved drive and form sheltered garden courts with benches, where visitors can sit near the crypt walls. Bands of light and dark granite run across the fronts, and smaller niche walls with planters bring the scale down along the walk."},"mek-smc":{"txt":"St. Mary Church in Pittsburgh becomes a place of remembrance, with interior crypt walls and a memorial garden. Inside, tall wood-faced crypt walls stand free under the vaulted ceiling, leaving the brick walls and stained glass windows in view. Outside, a brick archway leads visitors from the church into a garden of lawns, paths and low crypt walls."},"mek-spp":{"txt":"A crypt addition at Sts. Peter and Paul Cemetery in Naperville, Illinois. Two crypt buildings in red brick and green stone flank a domed shrine with a glass roof and a cross on top. The buildings sit around a circular court off the cemetery drive, where families can park close by and walk straight in."},"mek-sun":{"txt":"A cemetery garden, pavilion and administration building at Sunset Hill in Glen Carbon, Illinois. A stream runs downhill from the building through rocks and plantings, with paths on both sides and a small wood footbridge at the bottom. At the top, a terrace with a timber pergola gives families a place to stand and look out over the garden."},"str-cul":{"txt":"The Culinary Arts Lab at Rich South is a teaching kitchen with a dining lab next door. Students cook at rows of stainless steel work tables in front of a commercial cooking line, with windows along one side. The dining lab has a whiteboard wall and serving tables where they can plate and present what they made."},"str-d227":{"txt":"A new concession and ticket building stands at the stadium entry for District 227. One long white brick wall bends across the plaza and frames two gateways, marked Home and Visitors, with ticket windows between them. Past the gates, a paved court with red umbrella tables sits beside the track, so fans have a place to gather before they find a seat."},"str-oo":{"txt":"This 3-story renovation of Old Orchard Junior High School in Skokie adds new design elements, finishes and ceilings. The corridors get carpet with blue accents, blue lockers, wood doors and bright new ceilings, alongside brick walls and a mosaic mural."},"str-rc":{"txt":"This commons and cafeteria addition at Reed-Custer High School opens through tall windows to a covered patio with outdoor tables. Inside, ring lights hang over round cafeteria tables, and wood panels and a large school mural warm up the block walls. One building model drove both the construction documents and the views shared with the client."},"sg-balt":{"txt":"The dining decks of a harbor cruise vessel are reworked as one two-level room, with an open well between the decks. Guests at the upper rail look down on the tables below and across to a bar at each level. Tables and a buffet line run along the windows, with daylight coming in on both sides."},"sg-enr":{"txt":"The Enrichment Center is a learning and activity space for young people. Bench seating with turf tops, work tables and a large screen share one open room under a pitched ceiling. Pegboard walls, workbenches along the windows and a checkered floor fit the room for building, watching or sitting together."},"sg-hcal":{"txt":"The dining room of a harbor cruise vessel in California holds a long bar, banquet seating and a dance floor under a raised ceiling. High windows in the raised section bring daylight down to the dance floor and a grand piano beside it. The room is set for an evening sailing, with city lights in the windows."},"sg-hent":{"txt":"The dining deck of a harbor cruise vessel holds banquet seating, a bar and a buffet wall. Windows run the length of both sides, so nearly every table has a view of the water. The room is set for dinner, with the skyline in the windows."},"sg-lady":{"txt":"The dining salon of a charter yacht is planned around a bar, long banquet tables and window seating. Wood plank floors run underfoot, glassware hangs over the bar, and the city skyline fills the wide windows. The room is set for a private event."},"sg-mys":{"txt":"The dining room of a Chicago lake cruise vessel holds banquet tables and a bar under a lit ceiling cove that washes the room in soft blue. A patterned tile wall stands beside the bar, places are set at every table, and the lakefront fills the windows."},"sg-nor":{"txt":"The interior of a dining vessel in Norfolk holds a bar, a lounge and a dining deck. Guests can sit at the tile-fronted bar, settle into the lounge sofa or take a table along the windows. The windows run the length of the dining deck, with city lights across the water at dusk."},"sg-ody":{"txt":"Odyssey is a glass-enclosed dining vessel on the Chicago River. The glass walls and roof keep the skyline in view from every table, with a bar at one end of the dining room and an open deck with standing tables outside. The boat sits low on the river among the downtown towers."},"wha-120":{"txt":"Floors 23 and 24 of 120 South LaSalle in Chicago hold new tenant amenities and a roof terrace. An open stair beside tall windows links the two levels and leads to a lounge with a bar and game tables. Outside, the terrace carries deck seating, a planted green wall and a shade structure, with the downtown skyline on every side."},"wha-1sw":{"txt":"At 1 South Wacker in Chicago, the work covers the lobby reception, tenant lounge and conference center. In the lobby, a long white desk carries the building name against dark stone walls. Elsewhere, a round reception desk sits under a circular wood ceiling, with lounge seating and glass-fronted meeting rooms close by."},"wha-200j":{"txt":"The repositioning of this Loop office building starts at the sidewalk, where a new glass entry and canopy mark the address and open onto a brighter lobby. The tenant lounge holds long shared tables, soft seating by the windows and a bar under a wood slat ceiling, with planters throughout."},"wha-222":{"txt":"The entry plaza, canopy, lobby and tenant lounge at 222 South Riverside Plaza in Chicago are reworked from the street in. Steps and planted terraces rise from the sidewalk to a lit canopy over the doors. Inside, the lobby is pale stone and glass, and the lounge centers on a long fireplace set in a wood wall, with a cafe counter nearby and a ceiling of hexagonal panels."},"wha-2pp":{"txt":"At 2 Pierce Place, the lobby, game lounge and tenant amenities were reworked together. A curved blue wall carrying the building name leads people in from the lobby. Beyond it sit shuffleboard, pool and foosball tables, bright yellow window nooks and a lounge with deep sofas around a fireplace."},"wha-300w":{"txt":"These are office interiors at 300 South Wacker in Chicago, including a speculative suite. Glass-fronted conference rooms face the open office, so daylight and city views reach the desks. A cafe with bar-height and table seating gives staff a place to gather, warmed by an orange accent wall and a cluster of globe pendants."},"wha-332":{"txt":"The historic lobby at 332 South Michigan in Chicago is renewed, and a full floor becomes an amenities center with a fitness center, Wi-Fi lounge, elevator lobby and main stair. The lobby sets white marble walls against its ornate gilded ceiling. The amenities floor holds a lounge with a fireplace and game tables, and locker rooms finished in blue mosaic tile."},"wha-555":{"txt":"At 555 West Monroe in Chicago, the renovation of floors 1, 2 and 17 adds a new lobby, cafe, conference center, fitness center and roof deck. The lobby sets lounge seating and a cafe counter under a faceted ceiling hung with glass pendants. The fitness center faces an outdoor terrace through full-height glass."},"wha-701":{"txt":"This tenant roof deck sits on top of an office building. Shade canopies, planters, lounge seating and a bar counter with red stools make the roof an outdoor room for lunch and after-work events. A glass railing keeps the view open, and flowering planters and trees line the edges."},"wha-aae":{"txt":"These Chicago office interiors cover the reception, boardroom, cafe and open office. Reception centers on a wood and marble desk beside a slatted screen that gives a glimpse of the workspace beyond. The boardroom seats a large group at one long table with city views, and the cafe sets banquettes and round tables under globe pendants."},"wha-arbor":{"txt":"This cafe and tenant lounge serves a suburban office building. A sweeping curved ceiling and a long counter organize the room, with booth, table and lounge seating beneath the exposed structure. A skyline mural runs along the back wall, and the room includes a shuffleboard table."},"wha-butt":{"txt":"At 1333 Butterfield, a suburban office building, the shared tenant amenities sit inside the exposed concrete shell. Tenants get a lounge with soft seating and games, a self-serve cafe market, and a long communal counter under the exposed structure. Yellow accent walls and warm wood furniture brighten the concrete, and a pool table sits at the far end of the lounge."},"wha-chee":{"txt":"The office interiors for Cheetah Digital cover the reception, open office and cafe. A wood slat ceiling runs from the elevators to a green reception desk and a small seating area by the windows. Wood floors carry through to the open office, and the cafe holds a long island with stools for breaks and casual meetings."},"wha-chest":{"txt":"Chestnut Place gains an amenity lounge, a game room and shared work space. White ceiling fins hang over dark wood floors and carry from room to room. The floor holds a glass-fronted conference room, a pool table and lounge seating beside the kitchen counter."},"wha-fulc":{"txt":"At 250 East Wisconsin in Milwaukee, the work covers the storefront entry, lobby and tenant lounge. A lit canopy sign marks the entry from the sidewalk, and the white lobby is set off by a red reception desk and red lounge chairs. The tenant lounge is a round room with a curved sofa, colorful ottomans and a cafe counter."},"wha-glen":{"txt":"1000 Milwaukee Avenue is an office building in Glenview, Illinois, repositioned with a new glass entry pavilion. The pavilion leads to a skylit atrium that holds a reception desk, lounge seating and a cafe for tenants. Curved glass at the entry and round ceiling canopies inside soften the original building's straight lines."},"wha-henr":{"txt":"These are office and showroom interiors for a furniture dealer in Itasca, Illinois. The open office is organized by brightly colored volumes under the exposed roof structure, so the workspace doubles as a working display of the product. Glass-fronted rooms inside the red, yellow and blue volumes keep meetings visible from the desks."},"wha-hl3":{"txt":"Highland Landmark III is an office building in Downers Grove, Illinois, with an upgraded lobby, cafe and fitness center for its tenants. The two-story lobby pairs wood panels with a crystal chandelier and a curved lounge group. The cafe adds a long shared table and a green banquette by the windows, and the fitness center carries a bold red patterned wall."},"wha-hsbc":{"txt":"The workplace interiors for HSBC in Arlington Heights, Illinois, cover the open office, the collaboration areas and the corridors. Long rows of shared desks sit beside glass-fronted meeting rooms, and lounge seating with a fireplace and a kitchen counter offers a place away from the desk. Bands of color in the carpet follow the corridors across the floor."},"wha-mac":{"txt":"These office interiors for the MacArthur Foundation include a cafe, the reception area and conference rooms. Visitors arrive at a wood reception desk beside an open stair with a black metal railing, with a ring of armchairs for waiting. The cafe sits under a warm wood ceiling with a serving counter and small tables, and the conference rooms have glass fronts that keep them open to the floor."},"wha-meade":{"txt":"The headquarters interiors for Meade Electric in Willowbrook, Illinois, cover the reception area, the open office and the cafe. Reception sets a wood wall carrying the company name over a polished concrete floor, beside a row of high windows. The open office runs under the exposed roof structure with shared tables between workstations, and the cafe holds a full kitchen, high tables and a banquette along the glass."},"wha-ond":{"txt":"One North Dearborn in Chicago gains a tenant amenity floor, a fitness center and a roof deck. The lounge sits under exposed red steel trusses, with sofas, a bar and booth seating for meeting or working away from the desk. On the roof, lounge furniture, umbrellas and planters face the downtown skyline. The fitness center leaves its ducts and concrete columns in view."},"wha-ott":{"txt":"The atrium lobby, the entry canopy and the plaza of an office tower in Oakbrook Terrace, Illinois, are reworked in this study. Outside, a curved canopy and a fountain mark the front door, and a terrace with tables and red umbrellas gives tenants a place to sit. Inside, the tall atrium is tested two ways, one with hanging colored cubes and one with a crystal chandelier."},"wha-ott25":{"txt":"25 Ottawa in Grand Rapids, Michigan, is a heavy-timber loft building repositioned as office space, with work on the exterior, lobby, fitness center and office floors. The red brick shell and arched windows stay, with new storefronts and a patio at the sidewalk. Inside, the original timber posts and beams are left exposed through the lobby, the gym and the open office floors."},"wha-p44":{"txt":"The interiors for Project 44 cover the open office, a lounge and a game room. The lounge gathers sofas around a planted green wall and a chandelier, right beside the desks. Concrete columns and exposed ductwork run throughout, a wall clad like a shipping container adds color, and the game room sets a ping pong table next to the kitchen island."},"wha-pfz":{"txt":"The workplace interiors for the Pfizer H1 site consolidation cover the cafe, the atrium, the open office and the break areas. A cafe counter sits in the tall concrete atrium with bright blue and yellow chairs around it, and the dining room runs a long counter along the windows. On the office floors, break areas with kitchenettes and soft seating sit close to the desks."},"wha-pp":{"txt":"Presidents Plaza in Chicago is an office property renovated with a new lobby, a two-story fitness center, a restaurant and bar, and a cafe. The bar opens directly off the lobby, and the lounge beyond is furnished like a club room, with leather sofas, bookshelves and globe chandeliers. In the fitness center, wide steps link the reception level to a turf training floor below."},"wha-river":{"txt":"These lobby and common area improvements are for an office building in Rosemont, Illinois. The schemes add a sculptural reception desk, a hanging light feature and new lounge seating to the existing two-story space. White brick walls keep the room bright, and curved benches in orange, green and blue give visitors an easy place to wait near the front desk."},"wha-sal":{"txt":"The office interiors for The Salvation Army in Hoffman Estates, Illinois, include an assembly space, a cafe lounge, the lobby and a stair. The assembly space sets rows of chairs around a low platform under a wood ceiling. In the cafe lounge, round ceiling discs hang over soft seating and a red kettle mural, and the lobby stair rises beside a tall panel lettered with the mission."},"wha-shaf":{"txt":"One Shafer, at 6400 Shafer Court in Rosemont, Illinois, is a repositioning of the entry, lobby, tenant lounge and terrace. A new sign frames the revolving door at the top of the entry steps, and the two-story lobby gains a central seating group. The tenant lounge has a reclaimed wood nook and globe chandeliers, and its glass wall opens onto a terrace with a stone feature wall."},"wha-vail":{"txt":"Vail Apartments is a residential development on a sloped site. The apartments sit on stone bases, with timber gables and balconies stepping along the slope and a parking structure attached. The roofline was checked against the slope in a massing model, and a unit bedroom opens through a wide window to the mountain."},"wha-warr":{"txt":"These are lobby renovation options for an office building in Lisle, Illinois. Each option keeps the view through to the entry and changes the wall finishes, seating and lighting, so the owner could compare them side by side. One wraps the wall in light wood with red swivel chairs, and another uses white stone, purple chairs and a cluster of pendant lights."},"wha-willis":{"txt":"These speculative office suites in Willis Tower in Chicago were built out to lease ready to use. Each suite centers on a shared cafe and lounge under a curved ceiling, with screens and bright furniture marking places to meet. A teal wall and copper pendants anchor the kitchen island, and the desks are arranged around the cafe."},"wha-windy":{"txt":"Windy Point is a suburban office building with new shared tenant amenities: a lounge, a cafe and a fitness center. The lounge and cafe share bright pink accent walls and a mix of soft chairs and cafe tables, with cone pendants hanging over the cafe. The fitness center lines its treadmills up facing the windows and the trees outside."},"wha-wood":{"txt":"Woodland Falls is an office building in Mettawa, Illinois, with a lobby enhancement and a new tenant lounge. The two-story lobby gets a warmer entry wall and seating, and the lounge adds a cafe counter and places to work away from the desk. In the lounge, a curved sofa faces a pair of fireplaces, with a patterned ceiling panel floating over the tables."},"m2-gallatin":{"txt":"A two-story retail building on Gallatin Avenue in Nashville. Gray metal panels in three tones wrap the upper floor inside a green frame. A brick retaining wall with a stair and ramp separates the building from the parking below."},"mca-conc":{"txt":"A concession interior in Evanston with a coffered ceiling, a white counter and blue tile behind the service line. White plank walls and pendant lights run through the room, and a wall of windows and glass doors opens to the grounds outside."},"bf-tomi":{"txt":"A food hall stall in Chicago. A skyline cut from white panels rises behind the counter with the name in gold, over a pale wood front and black tile. Stools line a ledge along the side wall under linear lights."},"m2-wood":{"txt":"A three-story house built on a steep infill lot. White and gray volumes step back from the street behind a red fin wall, with the garage at grade and balconies above. Inside, the red wall carries through the main floor as a single plane that ties the living room, kitchen and open steel stair together."},"wha-125w":{"txt":"A new street entry for the office tower on Wacker Drive, studied in four options. Each sets a white canopy and a glass vestibule against the dark stone base, reaching out over the sidewalk below the tower's vertical piers. The options differ in the width and framing of the canopy."},"wha-225w":{"txt":"A new storefront at the corner of the tower base. Tall glass set between the stone piers opens the lobby to the sidewalk, with wood-toned walls and shelving lit behind it. Planters of red flowers run along the stone balustrade at the curb."},"wha-33d":{"txt":"Four options for a typical elevator lobby in the office tower. Each ends the corridor with a different focal wall: a metal screen, back-lit glass, wood paneling or artwork. The ceiling changes with each scheme, from a recessed light cove to a slatted wood soffit."},"wha-10120":{"txt":"Elevator lobby options for the two Riverside Plaza buildings. Dark wood or white panels line the walls between the elevator doors, with a looped light fixture overhead and patterned gray carpet underfoot. A window at the end of each lobby looks out to the city."},"wha-ajg":{"txt":"A gut renovation of a 315,000 SF building at 2850 Golf Road for the company's global headquarters. Blue glass and vertical fins replace the old facade, and the company name sits at the roofline. The program added a new front entrance, dining, a fitness club, a cafe and a rooftop terrace."},"wha-tri":{"txt":"Five office buildings totaling 559,204 SF sit at the Tri-State Tollway and Half Day Road, renovated in 2014 with Trammell Crow Company as developer. The white, stepped buildings line the tollway on one side and look across a tree-ringed pond on the other."},"wha-ap35":{"txt":"A four-story office campus set behind a broad lawn. Tan masonry buildings with long bands of windows step across the site, and rounded glass bays mark their corners. Mature trees and planting beds line the entry drive."},"wha-alpc":{"txt":"Two options for an office lobby in Cleveland. Stone-clad columns and a long curved reception desk stand in front of the glass wall in both. One scheme pairs black lounge chairs with a red artwork; the other sets a seating group on an orange rug beneath an oversized floor lamp."},"wha-abb":{"txt":"Master plan study for the North Chicago campus. Older buildings give way to a central green, with new buildings and parking at its edges. Paths cross the lawn between the buildings, and rows of trees screen the parking lots."},"wha-cta":{"txt":"Workplace interiors under an exposed concrete beam ceiling. Low workstations fill the open office, with purple and green accent walls at the core. The break room sets a green wall opposite a long run of cabinets, and the elevator lobby carries a blue wall crossed by white bands."},"wha-tta":{"txt":"Atrium lounge and elevator lobby for a five-story, 118,000 SF office building, part of a renovation of the main lobby, atrium and restrooms. In the atrium, a counter with blue stools and a seating group on a round orange rug sit below the open balconies. The elevator lobby is white, with red benches along its walls."},"wha-ohare":{"txt":"Common areas for an office building near O'Hare. The reception desk sits on a black-and-white chevron floor against a yellow-green wall. The cafe lines up a bar counter and tables with green chairs, and the tenant lounge sets dark banquettes under a grid of square light panels."},"wha-231":{"txt":"An amenities center for a historic bank building, with a fitness center, a tenant lounge and a roof deck. The lounge sets a linear fireplace in a paneled wall under clusters of globe pendants, with red chairs beside the tall windows. The fitness center lines its cardio machines along the window wall."},"wha-zur":{"txt":"Competition entry for the Zurich North America headquarters in Schaumburg. Long, low bars banded in glass and white metal stack and step along the site, and the company logo marks the end wall of the upper bar."},"wha-pfz3":{"txt":"Break areas and cafes for a workplace master plan. Faceted white walls fold around the pantries under an open black ceiling, with teal alcoves for seating. Island counters with stools anchor each pantry, branching pendant lights hang above them, and a geometric carpet in gray and aqua runs down the corridor."},"wha-cp1":{"txt":"Three options for a lobby coffee bar. A counter with a patterned tile front and a row of stools sits in a recess beside a refrigerated case, with small pendants above. The surround changes from cream walls to a blue frame between options."},"sg-burrell":{"txt":"Office suite with glass-fronted rooms around an open center. Black frames, white walls and a dark ceiling run through the conference room and private offices. A long table and a wall-mounted screen furnish the conference room, and a blue-gray patterned carpet continues under the glass."}};